# Generation 3, round 4, X-01 (generations/gen003/PLAN.md, version 4, the second wide screen). Chasing takers.
# Over each weekly bin (bars opening Monday 00:00 to Sunday 23:00 UTC): the taker-buy VWAP (taker-buy quote volume
# over taker-buy base volume) minus the taker-sell VWAP (the rest of the week's volume), over the week's range (high
# minus low). g > 0: takers bought at higher prices than they sold within the week (they bought more as the price
# rose: positive feedback); g < 0: takers bought dips and sold rallies. x = the week's log return in units of the
# coin's annualised daily volatility over n days. z = g net of a cross-sectional fit on x on every bin, so the book
# is neither a reversal nor a continuation book on the week's move. Short the largest z, long the smallest; rank
# weights, dollar neutral, gross 1; visible at the bar that opens Sunday 23:00, traded at the Monday 00:00 open.
# No funding, mark or index input.
name = "gen003_x01_taker_vwap_gap"
family = "flow"
kind = "portfolio"
unit = "top30"
hypothesis = "Positive-feedback takers: where takers bought at higher prices than they sold within the week, beyond what the week's move explains, momentum-chasing market orders set the price, and it gives back that chase premium over the next weeks; where takers bought dips and sold rallies, the price is held by patient value traders. Short chasers, long dip-buyers, weekly. Falsified if the DEV screen fails (sign never flipped), VAL PSR(0) < 0.90, 2x costs negative, no G6 timing, or next30 disagrees."

n = param(28, 22, 34)          # days of daily volatility that scale the week's move

bq = weekly(taker_buy_quote_volume)
bv = weekly(taker_buy_volume)
q = weekly(quote_volume)
v = weekly(volume)
g = (bq / bv - (q - bq) / (v - bv)) / (weekly(high) - weekly(low))
x = tf_last(logret(weekly(close), 1) / realised_vol(daily(close), n), weekly)
gd = cs_demean(g)
xd = cs_demean(x)
z = gd - cs_mean(xd * gd) / cs_mean(xd * xd) * xd
signal = cs_scale(cs_demean(-cs_rank(z)))
